## 2) Brief Justification for Each Service

| Service | Why it is used in this project |
|---|---|
| Amazon API Gateway | Provides a managed, secure API layer for frontend endpoints and routes requests to `api_handler` Lambda. |
| AWS Lambda | Runs backend compute units (`api_handler`, `feature_extraction`, `insight_generator`, `feedback_processor`, `training_check`, `model_trainer`) without server management. |
| AWS Step Functions | Orchestrates the multi-step audio and training pipelines with retries, branching, and failure handling. |
| Amazon S3 | Stores uploaded audio, frontend assets, Terraform state, and model artifacts. |
| Amazon DynamoDB | Stores child profiles, sessions, feedback, training features, and model version metadata. |
| Amazon Cognito | Provides managed user authentication and integrates with API Gateway authorizer for protected routes. |
| Amazon CloudFront | Delivers frontend static content with CDN caching and HTTPS. |
| Amazon VPC | Runs Lambda functions in private networking boundaries for controlled egress and better security posture. |
| Amazon NAT Gateway | Provides outbound internet/AWS-public-endpoint access from private subnets for services that do not use gateway endpoints in this design (for example Transcribe/other public service APIs). |
| Public IPv4 (Elastic IP) | Required network attachment for NAT Gateway operation. |
| AWS IAM | Enforces least-privilege access between compute, storage, orchestration, and AI services. |
| Amazon ECR | Stores versioned Lambda container images used in deployment workflows. |
| Amazon CloudWatch | Central monitoring for logs, metrics, alarms, and dashboarding. |
| Amazon SNS | Receives CloudWatch alarm actions and fans out operational notifications to subscribed channels (email now, extensible later). |
| Amazon EventBridge | Executes scheduled workflow triggers (such as daily training checks). |
| AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store | Stores runtime configuration references outside source code. |
| Amazon Bedrock | Supports model-based narrative generation path for parent-facing insight text (feature/config dependent). |
| Amazon Transcribe | Performs speech-to-text conversion for linguistic analysis flow. |
| Amazon SageMaker Serverless Inference | Hosts HuBERT endpoint for Advanced-mode acoustic inference. |
| AWS X-Ray | Captures distributed traces across Lambda and Step Functions for performance and debugging analysis. |

## 3) Resource Optimization Strategies

| Optimization Strategy | Status | Comment |
|---|---|---|
| DynamoDB on-demand (`PAY_PER_REQUEST`) | Implemented | Avoids overprovisioning and idle capacity cost. |
| S3 lifecycle policy (archive + expiration) | Implemented | Reduces long-term storage cost automatically. |
| CloudFront `PriceClass_100` | Implemented | Lower CDN cost profile for DEV usage. |
| ECR image retention policy (keep last 10 images) | Implemented | Controls registry storage growth. |
| Log retention control (DEV = 30 days) | Implemented | Prevents unbounded log retention cost. |
| VPC gateway endpoints for S3 and DynamoDB | Implemented | Avoids unnecessary NAT data path for these services. |
| Keep Advanced mode off by default (`use_sagemaker_intent_endpoint=false`) | Implemented | Prevents accidental inference cost in normal DEV usage. |
| Single-AZ DEV deployment (`us-east-1a`) | Implemented | Reduced NAT/IPv4 fixed baseline versus previous 2-AZ DEV setup. |
| Remove NAT entirely in DEV | Not implemented | NAT is still enabled because private-subnet workloads may require outbound access paths. |

